cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these computations, please cite this repository."
title: "Open Problems Lab: reproducible computations on open problems in number theory and combinatorics"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Small, checkable computations on open problems in number theory and combinatorics,
  mostly from erdosproblems.com. Each note is a reproduction of published values, a finite
  computation past the published range, or a negative result, with the scripts, outputs and
  an AI referee re-run report. The work was computed and re-run by AI agents and has not
  been reviewed by a human mathematician. Nothing here is a proof or a prize claim.
authors:
  - family-names: Lie
    given-names: Juwen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1384-7901"
keywords:
  - number theory
  - combinatorics
  - Erdos problems
  - reproducible computation
  - computational mathematics
repository-code: "https://github.com/juw12/open-problems-lab"
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
